A.mc("e2-c10-standard-2-check","c10-2-core","Which connection correctly explains the deep-vent food web in the source?",["*Bacteria use chemical energy that supports other organisms|The vent community depends on bacteria using chemicals such as hydrogen sulfide.", "Tube worms require sunlight reaching the abyssal bottom|The source explicitly contrasts deep vents with sunlight-supported surface ecosystems.", "All animals feed directly on liquid magma|Magma supplies heat, not the stated food source.", "The mineral plume is smoke from burning plants|The plume contains precipitated minerals, not plant-combustion smoke."],"Keep the heat source, circulating fluid, mineral precipitation and biological energy source distinct.",["TB10:10.2"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C10S2"]});
A.mc("e2-c10-standard-2-visual","c10-2-core","Compare the two ridge profiles. What best explains the deeper axial rift of the slower-spreading end member?",["*Cooling strengthens crust enough for larger normal faults|The source associates slower spreading with cooling, strength and fault-bounded relief.", "Slower spreading eliminates crustal extension|Both profiles represent divergent boundaries.", "The center is a trench where one plate subducts|An axial rift is not a subduction trench.", "Sediment turns into magma throughout the ridge|That is not the mechanism described in the source."],"Read the profile as the combined effect of spreading, magmatism, cooling and faulting.",["TB10:10.2"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C10S2"], "media": [{"kind": "img", "src": "animations/chapter10/source/10.2-p3-Im3.png", "alt": "Supplied section 10.2 course figure, PDF page 3", "cap": "Exploring Geology · 10.2 · PDF p3 · original source figure, unchanged geometry"}], "sourceFigure": true});
A.match("e2-c10-standard-2-bank","c10-2-core","Match the complete bank to these source-supported observations or relationships. A bank term may be used more than once when two observations share the same classification.",[["Lava erupts under seawater", "Pillow basalt"], ["Magma freezes in a narrow fracture", "Dike"], ["Extension moves a crustal block down", "Normal fault"], ["Hot water cools and precipitates sulfides", "Black-smoker mineral deposition"], ["Bacteria use chemical energy at depth", "Chemically supported vent ecosystem"]],"Spreading creates crust; circulating seawater builds a different mineral system.",["TB10:10.2"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C10S2"], "wordBank": true, "sourceFigure": false});
