A.mc("e2-c10-standard-8-check","c10-8-core","Which condition is necessary for the growing reef to remain shallow while its volcanic foundation subsides in Darwin’s model?",["*Upward reef growth keeps pace with relative submergence|That is the condition that preserves the shallow reef rim.", "The entire reef sinks at the same rate without growth|That would tend to drown the reef rather than maintain its shallow rim.", "The underlying volcano must continue to rise forever|The model explicitly includes a subsiding volcanic foundation.", "All carbonate dissolves before a lagoon can form|A persistent carbonate reef is essential to this model."],"Keep the upward construction and downward foundation motion separate.",["TB10:10.8"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C10S8"]});
A.mc("e2-c10-standard-8-visual","c10-8-core","Compare the three source stages. Which change creates the lagoon separating the later reef from the remaining island?",["*The island subsides as the reef continues upward growth|The source sequence develops a barrier and lagoon around the shrinking island.", "The whole ring moves down without adding carbonate|That fails to preserve the shallow growing reef in the sequence.", "A trench cuts through the center of an active arc|The source is an atoll model, not a subduction cross section.", "A salt dome pushes the island through the reef|Salt deformation is not part of the depicted mechanism."],"The sequence combines biological construction with thermal subsidence.",["TB10:10.8"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C10S8"], "media": [{"kind": "img", "src": "animations/chapter10/source/10.8-p4-Im7.png", "alt": "Supplied section 10.8 course figure, PDF page 4", "cap": "Exploring Geology · 10.8 · PDF p4 · original source figure, unchanged geometry"}], "sourceFigure": true});
A.match("e2-c10-standard-8-bank","c10-8-core","Match the complete bank to these source-supported observations or relationships. A bank term may be used more than once when two observations share the same classification.",[["Reef attached to or close to a shoreline", "Fringing reef"], ["Reef separated from land by a lagoon", "Barrier reef"], ["Reef ring enclosing a lagoon", "Atoll"], ["Broad shallow carbonate accumulation", "Carbonate platform"], ["Lowering of a cooling volcanic foundation", "Subsidence"]],"An atoll can preserve shallow-water growth above a sinking volcanic foundation.",["TB10:10.8"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C10S8"], "wordBank": true, "sourceFigure": false});
