A.mc("e2-c10-standard-11-check","c10-11-core","Why does an enlarging Atlantic not require Earth’s surface area to increase?",["*Oceanic lithosphere can be consumed by subduction elsewhere|Creation and destruction can redistribute ocean-basin area.", "Every continent must dissolve into the ocean|That is not the plate-tectonic area balance.", "New oceanic crust has no area|Spreading produces real lithosphere.", "The Pacific contains no convergent boundaries|The source describes substantial surrounding subduction."],"Distinguish redistribution of plate area from expansion of the whole planet.",["TB10:10.11"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C10S11"]});
A.mc("e2-c10-standard-11-visual","c10-11-core","Compare the 150 Ma and 120 Ma reconstructions. Which relative relationship is supported?",["*The Central Atlantic is established before the South Atlantic fully opens|The source panels place these openings in different stages.", "Every Atlantic sector opened at exactly the same time|That contradicts the sequence.", "India had already completed its collision with Asia at 150 Ma|The reconstruction places that collision much later.", "The panels show only a single side of Earth|The source explicitly describes an oval world map."],"Use the actual panel ages and continental positions rather than assuming a simultaneous split.",["TB10:10.11"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C10S11"], "media": [{"kind": "img", "src": "animations/chapter10/source/10.11-p3-Im3.png", "alt": "Supplied section 10.11 course figure, PDF page 3", "cap": "Exploring Geology · 10.11 · PDF p3 · original source figure, unchanged geometry"}, {"kind": "img", "src": "animations/chapter10/source/10.11-p4-Im4.png", "alt": "Supplied section 10.11 course figure, PDF page 4", "cap": "Exploring Geology · 10.11 · PDF p4 · original source figure, unchanged geometry"}], "sourceFigure": true});
